<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūnae</span></b> , ārum
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūna</span></b> ,
		ae, <i><span class="en">Prud. Dipt. 112</span></i>),
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cradle</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tune etiam cubitare solitu's in cunis puer?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 4, 7, 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus est cunis, incunabulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Truc. 5, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen. 23, 83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc.
				1, 39, 93</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 1, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6,
				167</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. M. 10, 392</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 2,
			31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 89</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11,
				39, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 94</span></i> et saep.—Of
				<i>the nests</i> of young birds, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 3,
				12, 10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, like our <i>cradle</i>, for <i>birth</i> or <i>earliest childhood</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				313</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 67</span></i>; cf. cunabula, II. B.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
